  "claim": "touch_imbalance_predicts_next_sign_measured",
  "interpretation": "Each signed event is scored against the touch imbalance at the prior book row. p_buy_slope_per_quintile is the OLS slope of P(next event = buy) across imbalance quintiles; a positive monotone gradient means queue skew anticipates the next event's direction. Quintile edges are pooled so the exec/submission-conditioned tables share bins. ZI-LOB arms re-use the same machinery on the sim's own book \u2014 its symmetric flows leave slope near zero unless a flow driver (regime/split) injects direction persistence.",
